                                                "sense_id": "a9dfcc49-26fe-30ad-a65a-01fcf01063f0",
                                                "text": "The sudden drop in temperature should alarm you into taking precautions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1079e56-862a-4219-9c11-d2a42716e77e",
                                                "sense_id": "a9dfcc49-26fe-30ad-a65a-01fcf01063f0",
                                                "text": "Her illness started to alarm the doctors, who ordered more tests."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac51e6ed-0087-4208-953c-903f00ef71c1",
                                                "sense_id": "a9dfcc49-26fe-30ad-a65a-01fcf01063f0",
                                                "text": "When the carriage drew up in the grass-grown court yard before the hall-door, two lazy-looking men, whose appearance well accorded with that of the place which they tenanted, alarmed by the obstreperous barking of a great chained dog, ran out from some half-ruinous out-houses, and took charge of the horses; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ebcb2c33-bfc4-3cd6-9db9-4376e212bea2",
                                        "entry_id": "c7b6a5fa-32b6-302b-b29a-8c146731f68a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To produce a warning of approaching danger or necessary action; to emit a signal intended to rouse a recipient to vigilance or put them on the alert."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4511a01-2f5c-4ede-8061-34fbc7501fff",
                                                "sense_id": "ebcb2c33-bfc4-3cd6-9db9-4376e212bea2",
                                                "text": "The tower cab supervisor and various pilots stated that the LLWAS system frequently alarms because of the thunderstorm activity present, and that airspeed losses are common as a result of convective wind shear."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7a331f1-2f15-3395-ad11-07ece8427e9e",
                                        "entry_id": "c7b6a5fa-32b6-302b-b29a-8c146731f68a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To surprise with apprehension of danger; to fill with anxiety in regard to threatening evil; to excite with sudden fear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09813173-7e57-4f3f-95c7-0b9055997dbd",
                                                "sense_id": "c7a331f1-2f15-3395-ad11-07ece8427e9e",
                                                "text": "The loud bang in the hallway seemed to alarm everyone in the building."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2188b08c-850a-334e-a6ef-f837b628a1fc",
                                        "entry_id": "c7b6a5fa-32b6-302b-b29a-8c146731f68a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To keep in excitement; to disturb."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
